      {
        "title": "Ask HN: If the models are so good, why doesn't OpenAI just start 100 companies?",
        "link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997",
        "description": "<p>Title is a bit of an exaggeration but the question is more: if the frontier models are so good, why even sell them as your primary money maker?<p>Couldn't OpenAI or Anthropic make a lot more money by just starting companies themselves that leverage the models and building their own products?<p>Is selling tokens really the best strategy?<p>Especially with commodification and prices declining wouldn't that indicate there is more money to be made on the application-side of the models rather than the utility side</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50200997</a></p>\n<p>Points: 391</p>\n<p># Comments: 431</p>",
